Creating an appropriate Conda environment on MacOS ARM64

On Mac:
conda create -n compmatmul doxygen cmake clang clangxx libcxx llvm-openmp catch2 pybind11 numpy

With FFTW:
conda create -n compmatmul-fftw doxygen cmake clang clangxx libcxx llvm-openmp catch2 fftw pybind11 numpy

On Linux:
conda create -n compmatmul doxygen cmake clang clangxx clangxx_linux-64 libcxx libcxxabi llvm-openmp catch2 mkl mkl-devel pybind11 numpy
conda install numpy "libblas=*=*_mkl"

With FFTW:
conda create -n compmatmul-fftw doxygen cmake clang clangxx libcxx libcxxabi catch2 mkl mkl-devel fftw libgomp pybind11 numpy

For building documentation:
cmake --build build --target docs


Installing FXT:
1. Download https://www.jjj.de/fxt/fxt-2026.05.19.tar.gz
2. make install PREFIX=${CONDA_PREFIX}



Importing the Python module with asan enabled:
On Mac:
ASAN_LIB="$(clang++ -print-file-name=libclang_rt.asan_osx_dynamic.dylib)"
DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES="$ASAN_LIB" python3 -c 'import compmatmul'

On Linux:
LD_PRELOAD=$(clang -print-file-name=libclang_rt.asan-x86_64.so) PYTHONMALLOC=malloc PYTHONPATH=. python3 ../tests.py